# Lessons

- When updating library metadata, make sure to check setup.py, README.md, and LICENSE files for author information and URLs.
- Repository and author information may be included in multiple places including badges, code examples, and documentation.
- When creating Docker files, ensure consistent directory structures between the host and container.
- Use multiple Docker files for different services (worker, tests) and coordinate them in docker-compose.yml.
- Docker volumes should be used for data persistence and sharing between containers.